WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.367
At least

00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:01.568
14 people have been

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.570
killed in Ukraine, including children,

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.705
after a deadly barrage of Russian missile

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:07.540
missile strikes across the country.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.242
CNN's Nic Robertson is live on the scene.

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:11.411
Human which is just south of Kiev.

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:13.113
Nick, I know this is the first strike in

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:15.215
or even around Kiev in a while, believe

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:16.983
since early March.

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:17.851
What can you tell us about

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:18.218
what's happened?

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:19.152
I know Ukraine had said

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:20.220
that they had intercepted

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.221
some of these, but what else?

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:22.088
What are you seeing on the damage

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:25.291
on the front Yeah.

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:27.827
The Ukrainian officials intercepted

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:29.162
most of those

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:31.364
missiles that were fired at Ukraine

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:32.732
and Kiev.

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:34.334
First time missiles were fired

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:35.235
on that city

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:37.704
in 51 days here in Oman

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:39.105
on some of the missiles

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:40.173
unfortunately got through.

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:42.709
This is a damage the rescue and recovery

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:44.010
they've been on this site

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:47.414
the missiles hit here about 9 hours ago.

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:48.281
If you look up there,

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:50.350
you can still see the smoke

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:53.486
coming out of the apartment building that

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:54.020
a missile

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:56.456
just slammed into this building.

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:58.525
We know that on site now.

00:00:58.525 --> 00:00:59.492
And while we've been here,

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:00.927
we've seen another two bodies

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:01.528
carried out.

00:01:01.528 --> 00:01:04.030
At least 15 people killed here.

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:06.366
We understand three of them children

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:07.700
we talked to an eyewitness

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.102
was one of the first people

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:09.936
on the scene here.

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:12.305
He said he could hear women and children

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:13.473
screaming in the rubble.

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:14.541
And I'm just going to walk you

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:16.176
through this rescue

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:17.510
and recovery operation

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.446
that's going on here right now.

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:21.147
There are fire trucks here

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:23.216
that are still putting water

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:25.085
on the blaze.

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:27.253
And if you follow me across here,

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.655
David, David's our camera

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:30.523
and follow me across here.

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:31.925
The families here

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:33.860
still waiting to find out

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.995
what's happened to their loved ones.

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:37.597
As you come around here,

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:38.965
you just get to see

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:42.135
how bad the devastation is

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:44.104
There's a line of firemen.

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:44.370
I don't know

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.405
if David, you can get in

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:46.539
to see them behind me,

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:48.374
but there's a line of firemen

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:49.776
scouring the ground there

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.277
where that digger is trying

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:53.279
to pull the rubble out.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:54.781
This is an apartment building

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:57.851
that has 46 different apartments in it.

00:01:57.851 --> 00:01:59.185
The missile strike here

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:00.954
at 5:00 in the morning

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:02.155
while people were sleeping.

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:05.258
So most of the victims so far,

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:06.126
we understand,

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:07.794
were all asleep in their beds.

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.295
There are dozens injured.

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:10.063
And frankly,

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:11.865
we've been talking to the officials here

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:12.632
They still don't

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:15.502
have a real, real accurate figure

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:16.836
of how many people

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:17.871
they're are still searching for.

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:18.538
One of the rescuers

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:20.206
we talked to a couple of minutes ago

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:21.474
told us they still believe

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:22.442
there's another

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:23.910
couple of children

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:24.344
in there

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:25.278
that they're trying to find

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:25.812
at the moment.

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:27.013
And there's a line of relatives

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:28.548
I'm looking at over there,

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:30.049
desperately waiting.

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:31.317
Distant just beyond

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:31.718
that big

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:34.787
crane there, desperately waiting for news

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.322
about their loved ones.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.625
This is a slow and difficult process.

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:40.560
Of course, Ukraine

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:41.928
and the officials here

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:43.897
very, very familiar

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:46.566
with these devastating Russian strikes.

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:49.068
No matter how many of those missiles

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:50.503
they shoot down,

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:53.373
a couple still managed to get through.

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:54.707
And this is a result of it.

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:56.976
It's just horrifying for this community.

00:02:56.976 --> 00:03:00.079
Yeah, you hear 21 of 23 intercepted

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:01.381
but look at the damage

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:03.483
of what did get through, what wasn't

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:05.018
successfully intercepted.

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:06.352
It speaks to, of course, when they say

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:08.321
they need defense systems for this.

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:08.621
But Nick,

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:09.189
I think what

00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:10.456
you're talking about

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:11.090
is waiting to hear

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:12.091
what happened to their loved ones.

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:13.326
You can even imagine

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:14.160
what they're going through.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.895
This is obviously a residential area.

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:16.496
It's what,

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:18.498
200 miles from the front line

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:19.832
of where the fighting actually goes.

00:03:22.235 --> 00:03:24.170
Oh, it's a huge distance

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:24.904
from the front line.

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:26.706
You're right. About 200 miles.

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:28.141
And I'm looking around.

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:29.976
I mean, this apartment building here,

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:31.544
we're told by officials

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:35.014
109 people are registered living in here.

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:36.249
But I'm just going to ask

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:38.117
David to give us a quick spin

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:40.220
around this neighborhood.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:40.954
And you see

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:42.722
how many other buildings are we?

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:44.824
We just look around here.

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:48.795
This is a dense residential neighborhood.

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:49.862
We're looking at here.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:50.730
All around

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:51.864
there are buildings,

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:53.399
thousands of people,

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:55.602
thousands upon thousands of people

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:56.636
living here.

00:03:56.636 --> 00:03:58.771
So even hundreds of miles

00:03:58.771 --> 00:03:59.572
from the front line

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:00.840
and here in this city, Omar,

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.342
one to what a local residents

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:02.842
was telling us,

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:04.711
they haven't had a missile strike here

00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:06.980
since March last year.

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:09.816
So for the people in these buildings

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:10.783
I'm looking at,

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:11.851
they're probably breathing

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:13.219
a sigh of relief

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:15.588
for the relatives desperately waiting.

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:17.323
But the reality for all of them,

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:18.691
it doesn't matter where you are

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:21.194
100 miles, 200, 300 from the front line.

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:24.764
You just don't know what can happen next.

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:26.966
Yeah. Absolute no sense of safety.

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:28.201
Nick, I know you'll be tracking this.

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:29.369
Will stay with you this morning.

00:04:29.369 --> 00:04:29.802
Thank you.

